<%- include('partials/header', { pageTitle: "About" }) %>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="container fluid-container">
    <h1>About <%= APP.NAME %></h1>
    <h2>Capture now. Sync later.</h2>
    <blockquote>
      <p class="quote-text">
        Your productivity shouldn't stop because your connection does.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Inboxios is an
      <strong> open-source, offline-first task manager</strong> designed to make
      task capture fast, reliable, and distraction-free. It integrates with
      Notion while ensuring that creating a task never depends on having a
      perfect internet connection.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="problem block-space-2xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>The Problem</h2>
    <p>
      Most productivity applications rely on a constant internet connection.
      Even a brief network interruption can slow down or completely interrupt
      your workflow.
    </p>
    <p>
      When your goal is simply to capture an idea before you forget it, waiting
      for an API request is unnecessary friction.
    </p>
    <p class="highlight"><strong><%= APP.NAME %></strong> aims to eliminate that friction.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="solution block-space-2xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>The Solution</h2>
    <p>Inboxios follows an <strong>offline-first</strong> approach.</p>
    <p>
      Every task is designed to be captured instantly and stored locally first.
      Synchronization with Notion happens separately, allowing you to continue
      working without interruption.
    </p>
    <p>This means you can:</p>
    <ul class="simple-list highlight">
      <li>Capture tasks instantly</li>
      <li>Continue working offline</li>
      <li>Synchronize changes when a connection becomes available</li>
      <li>Keep your workflow uninterrupted</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The application treats synchronization as a background process rather than
      something that blocks the user.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="working block-space-2xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How <%= APP.NAME %> Works</h2>
    <div class="flowchart">
      <div class="step">Create Task</div>
      <div class="step">Inboxios</div>
      <div class="step">Local Storage</div>
      <div class="step">Synchronization Queue</div>
      <div class="step">Notion API</div>
      <div class="step">Your Notion Workspace</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      The long-term goal is to make synchronization automatic and resilient,
      ensuring that your local data and Notion remain in sync with minimal user
      interaction.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tech-stack block-space-3xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Inboxios is built with a modern JavaScript stack focused on simplicity and
      maintainability.
    </p>
    <dl class="badge-list">
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">Node.js</dt>
        <dd class="description">JavaScript runtime</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">Express</dt>
        <dd class="description">Web framework</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">EJS</dt>
        <dd class="description">Server-side rendering</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">Axios</dt>
        <dd class="description">Communication with the Notion API</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">Notion API</dt>
        <dd class="description">Task storage and synchronization</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt class="term">CSS</dt>
        <dd class="description">Responsive user interface</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      The project intentionally avoids unnecessary complexity while maintaining
      a modular architecture.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reason block-space-2xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Why I Built <%= APP.NAME %></h2>
    <p>
      Inboxios began as a way to explore <strong>REST API</strong>s and backend development with
      Express.
    </p>

    <p>
      As the project grew, it became an opportunity to experiment with software
      architecture, server-side rendering, synchronization strategies, and
      building production-style web applications.
    </p>

    <p>
      Rather than simply connecting a frontend to an API, the goal is to
      understand how real-world applications are designed, structured, and
      maintained.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="open-source block-space-2xl">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Open Source</h2>
    <p>Inboxios is an <strong>open-source</strong> project.</p>

    <p>
      Whether you're looking to learn Express, explore the Notion API, or
      contribute ideas, you're welcome to explore the project.
    </p>
    <h3>Resources</h3>
    <div class="btn-group">
      <a
        href="<%= APP.LINKS.DOCS %>"
        class="btn btn-links"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Documentation</a
      >
      <a
        href="<%= APP.LINKS.GITHUB %>"
        class="btn btn-links"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >GitHub Repository</a
      >
      <a
        href="<%= APP.LINKS.ISSUES %>"
        class="btn btn-links"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Report an Issue</a
      >
      <a
        href="<%= APP.LINKS.TEMPLATE %>"
        class="btn btn-links"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Notion Template</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
